<!-- P3 heritage, a revisited range's call guards. No issue number: found while
     reviewing a float-return PR. `kills` (decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/floatcalls.c,
     gcc -O2 -mavx2) stores four float call results into a global with
     `vmovss %xmm0,sink`. Each VEX instruction writes the whole zmm0, so the
     first heritage pass guards each call over 64 bytes, and the store reads
     four of them, so RulePullsubIndirect narrows each call's creation of xmm0
     to those four. A later pass adds an argument read of the eight-byte
     XMM0_Qa at a call, which revisits that range for old addresses only:
     removeRevisitedMarkers turned each narrowed creation into a SUBPIECE of the
     range after the call, and no guard of the pass rebuilt the call's kill, so
     the store read the value from before the call: `i2f_div(..,5); sink = v7;`
     with v7 the loop's last float, and `twice(..)` dropped its result for the
     same reason. Heritage now guards each such call again over the whole range
     for its effect, and every result reaches its store. Correctness fix, no
     option; one pass, default settings. All five fail before the fix.
-->
